 "description": "Chaudhury2020 - EC50 expansion and killing mathematical model of CAR-T cell and tumour kinetics\nBioModels BIOMD0000001025 (curated). SBML file: Chaudhury2020 Eq 7-9.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 360 time units (SED-ML: Chaudhury2020 Eq 7-9 - Fig 3(A) simulation.sedml), sampling 0.3.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 3.81e-06 of species peak (worst: Persistent_CAR_T_cells)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] species 'CAR_T_cells' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] Tumor_cell_growth term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Tumor_cell_death: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] rate rule dPersistent_CAR_T_cells/dt term 4: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - Persistent_CAR_T_cells: zero order, signed",
 "settings": {
  "kpath": "",
  "switches": "-ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint",
  "nation": false
 },
